From ac5b0b0b9a9d075daa033c68397a150b16a1267a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Isaac Duarte <31712685+Isaac-Duarte@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:40:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/23] drm/apple: dcp-fabric: give T6050 DP IN 2 and 3 their
 own tunnel slots

A port's Thunderbolt DP tunnels are kept in two owner slots, primary and
secondary, and dcp_fabric_dpin_slot() maps DP IN n and n + 2 onto the same
one. That models the dual-stream DCPs, but on T6050 every pipeline drives a
single DP IN (fixed CRTCs), and the host router has four DP IN adapters. A
dock with three displays gets DP IN 0, 1 and 2; the third lands in DP IN 0's
occupied slot and is refused before any free pipeline is considered:

  apple-dcp 2b2e00000.dcp: port already routed, not taking DP tunnel dpin2
  thunderbolt-apple-acio 381ac0000.acio: dpin2: DP tunnel setup failed: -98

Widen the core port's owner array to one slot per DP IN, and let
dcp_fabric_tunnel_owner() pick a DP IN's slot: its stream slot as before,
or, with fixed CRTCs, the DP IN's own. dcp_fabric_tunnel_slot() takes the
same choice, so DP IN 2 and 3 are admitted by the one set of rules. The
driver's port keeps owner, secondary_owner and the new dpin_owner[] as views
of one slots[] array in the core's order, and every owner-slot lookup goes
through dcp_tb_slot() (attach, release, request finish, DP events). The
fabric snapshot, the port's HPD, connector binding and route unregistration
cover all four slots, and the Type-C mux path counts a tunnel in any slot
as holding the port, so a DP alt mode state is not applied to a port whose
DP IN 0 tunnel went first while DP IN 2's is still up.

dcp_tb_candidate() still takes the stream of DP IN 2/3 from its parity; it
only feeds the dual-stream pairing order, which fixed-CRTC machines do not
run.

The slot change follows the SoC (apple,t6050), so J716c gets it too; other
SoCs keep the two-slot mapping.

Tested on J714s (M5 Pro) with a Thunderbolt 5 dock (Ugreen 10-in-1) and
three 1080p displays, together with the J714s device tree change that gives
dcpext1 a route to the right port: DP IN 0, 1 and 2 go to dcpext0, dcpext1
and dcpext2, and all three displays light up, as they do on macOS. The
firmware accepts the DPTX DFP port of DP IN 2.

Signed-off-by: Isaac Duarte <31712685+Isaac-Duarte@users.noreply.github.com>
